'''Nichos Marr''' was an individual whose named was carved into the wall of a safehouse on the [[planet]] [[Mapuzo]]<ref name="Trivia">{{SW|url=obi-wan-kenobi-part-iii-trivia-gallery|text=Part III Trivia Gallery &#124; Obi-Wan Kenobi}}</ref> by [[9 BBY]].<ref name="Date">{{KenobiDate|III}}</ref> The safehouse was used by members of the [[Hidden Path]] to smuggle [[Force-sensitive]]s and other individuals away from the [[Galactic Empire]] to the planet [[Jabiim]], where they would be given new identities to go into hiding.<ref name="Kenobi3">{{Kenobi|Part III}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Nichos-torso.jpg|200px|thumb|Nichos Marr in the ''Star Wars'' Legends continuity]]
In the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]], Nichos Marr was mentioned in the trivia gallery of the episode guide for the [[Part III|third episode]] of the ''[[Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi]]'' television series,<ref name="Trivia" /> which aired on [[June 1]], [[2022]].<ref name="D23">{{D23|url=everything-new-you-can-stream-on-disney-in-june-2022|text=Everything New You Can Stream on Disney+ in June 2022}}</ref> The guide established that Marr's name was one of several references to characters from the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity carved into the wall of the safe house set for the episode,<ref name="Trivia" /> although his name is not one of the ones visible in the final episode.<ref name="Kenobi3">{{Kenobi|Part III}}</ref> In Legends, [[Nichos Marr/Legends|Nichos Marr]] was first mentioned in the [[1995]] novel [[Children of the Jedi (novel)|''Children of the Jedi'']] by [[Barbara Hambly]].<ref name="CotJ">[[Children of the Jedi (novel)|''Children of the Jedi'']]</ref>

